# clang-tidy config for Quakespasm PPC port.
# Round v6 (2026-05-09): noise-suppression sweep.
#
# scripts/analyze-all.sh enables a broad check list:
#   --checks='bugprone-*,performance-*,readability-*,cert-*,misc-*,
#             -readability-magic-numbers,
#             -readability-isolate-declaration,
#             -readability-braces-around-statements'
#
# This file layers further excludes on top, suppressing categories that
# don't surface real Quake bugs but dominate the log (~60K of the original
# ~70K lines). After this trim the log is ~1.5K lines of actually
# reviewable findings.
#
# Suppressed-and-rationale (counts from pre-suppression run, 2026-05-09):
#
#   bugprone-narrowing-conversions (6090) — Quake's vec3 / int↔float
#       idiom: scaling, fixed-point, RGB pack/unpack, time deltas. Each
#       cast is intentional. False-positive rate ≈ 100%.
#
#   misc-include-cleaner (5152) — header inclusion graph quibbles.
#       Quake's Quake/quakedef.h is the umbrella header by design;
#       refactoring per-file include lists is project-out-of-scope.
#
#   readability-identifier-length (2215) — Quake convention uses i, j,
#       k for loop counters; s, c, p for string/char/ptr; v for vec3.
#       Renaming would churn every file for no readability win.
#
#   readability-uppercase-literal-suffix (747) — `1.0f` vs `1.0F`. Style
#       preference; lowercase is universal in C since K&R. Pedantic.
#
#   readability-math-missing-parentheses (456) — `a + b * c` is fine.
#       Operator precedence is part of the language; parens-everywhere
#       hurts readability of the math-heavy mathlib.c paths.
#
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#       (239) — every memset/memcpy/sprintf flagged as "use _s variants".
#       _s variants don't exist on PowerPC Tiger/Panther toolchains and
#       the bounds are statically known at every call site we control.
#
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity (129) — Host_Frame, drawing
#       loops, message parsers — all famously long Quake functions.
#       Splitting them is a refactor, not a bug fix; out of scope.
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters (128) — fires on any function
#       with two same-typed args. Quake has many (vec3 src, vec3 dst).
#       False-positive rate ≈ 90%; not worth the noise.
#
#   readability-non-const-parameter (62) — flags non-const ptrs that the
#       function doesn't actually mutate. Adding const requires touching
#       headers + every caller; project-out-of-scope refactor.
#
#   misc-unused-parameters (37) — typically callbacks with fixed
#       signatures (cmd handlers, demo loaders). Renaming to _foo
#       silences but adds no value.
#
#   readability-else-after-return (30), readability-redundant-* (52),
#   readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name (18),
#   readability-avoid-* (26), readability-named-parameter (9) —
#       style-only; Quake codebase consistency wins over modern
#       clang-tidy preferences.
#
# Kept-and-why (these still surface in the log post-suppression):
#
#   bugprone-* (excluding the four above) — real-bug-prone patterns:
#       narrowing-via-multiplication, macro parentheses, switch fall-
#       through, suspicious string compares, branch clones, integer
#       division, suspicious realloc.
#   clang-analyzer-deadcode.DeadStores (19) — uninit / over-write paths.
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy (16) — real overflow risk.
#   performance-type-promotion-in-math-fn (21) — float vs double in
#       math.h calls; can reveal genuine perf-relevant precision bugs.

# Note: clang-tidy resolves checks as a glob list. The cmdline --checks=
# option REPLACES this whole Checks: setting (verified with clang-tidy 20
# --list-checks). So scripts/analyze-all.sh's clangtidy stage no longer
# passes --checks= at all — the effective list lives here as the single
# source of truth.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  cert-*,
  misc-*,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-unused-parameters,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix,
  -readability-math-missing-parentheses,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-non-const-parameter,
  -readability-redundant-casting,
  -readability-redundant-declaration,
  -readability-else-after-return,
  -readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator,
  -readability-avoid-unconditional-preprocessor-if,
  -readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name,
  -readability-named-parameter

# WarningsAsErrors blank — these are advisory.
WarningsAsErrors: ''

# header-filter remains 'Quake/' (set on the analyze-all.sh cmdline).
